PRETABLE ADDENDUM -- #548 revision 2 (after pass 2), written BEFORE table 3 runs (its mtime is the order proof)
==========================================================================================================

WHAT CHANGED and why (pass 2: the eight transports, the dedicated codex job, the Opus measuring seat)
  * M_cmp0 (`pending_bound[nr]` -> `pending_bound[0]` in footbridge_pending) passed EVERY row in the battery (Opus,
    measured): a weakened operand of the fix's own predicate against #442's shipped detectors -> L2.  It is the second
    label-axis escape after #442 pass 2's `[0]` store, so the repair closes the class: R6b arms all four timers at
    four DISTINCT rates and checks each one.
  * The drain block's four-timer claim was unpinned (codex x2, glm, kimi-sub), its rate/accrual unpinned (Opus: one
    hex digit, LOAD_RUN 0x100 -> 0x800, reads 381 with the bound removed and passes 28/28), and a probe edit that
    zeroes the drained count passed every row (codex dedicated).  L1: the rows are pre-ship.
  * R6's new cell could be undone by edits to the row itself (`&&` -> `||`, a smaller precharge; grok, minimax,
    codex panel).  L1: the owed counts are printed and gate 2 pins the printed line.

SECTION 4 (CHANNEL) CORRECTED -- codex panel, pass 2, and it is right
  The first PRETABLE said "controls prove ...: any control failing -> FBDRAIN_CONTROL=FAILED" and "probe exit status:
  VERDICT=FAIL or a failed control -> exit 1".  A FAILED control makes the probe print REPORT-ONLY, the verdict guard
  reds, and `continue` skips every later row for that timer: those two rows never run on a failed control.  Their
  channel there is "reached a verdict".  They still carry the verdict=FAIL case (exit 1) and a CONTROL line that
  contradicts a PASS.  And "hangs to the harness budget" named no watchdog: nothing outside the probe times it.  Its
  own budgets bound it (free_run's 20 s prompt waits, the 30 s drain, close()'s 20 s drain + 10 s reap).

